  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "10.8.0 -- a full accessibility audit of the UI Kit (58 findings, adversarially verified) plus an EditFile addition.\n\nBREAKING\n- IMessageService/INotificationService gain Pause(Guid)/Resume(Guid) (WCAG 2.2.1 toast auto-dismiss control). Source break only for a hand-written implementation of either interface -- the built-in MessageService/NotificationService and static Wasm facades already implement both, wired automatically from hover/focus.\n\nNEW\n- EditFile gains Bordered (wraps the field in a bordered card) and AllowDownload (file names become re-save links) -- matches Ant Design's already-uploaded-file card pattern.\n- Table gains AriaLabel/ScrollRegionLabel/LoadingLabel/SelectRowLabelFor/FilterAppliedButtonLabelFormat/FilterAppliedLabel and keyboard row activation (Enter, WCAG 2.1.1); Pagination gains Disabled/AnnounceTotal.\n- DatePicker/DateRangePicker: calendars are now real ARIA grids, FormatHintLabel, RTL-aware arrow keys, ArrowDown moves focus into the grid. Tabs also gain RTL-aware arrows.\n- Alert/toasts gain SeverityLabel/CloseButtonLabel/Live localization; Popover/Popconfirm get aria-label fallbacks; Modal/Drawer inert their background while open (data-wss-keep-interactive escape hatch); tooltips gain full AT exposure + Escape-dismiss (WCAG 1.4.13).\n- New --wss-color-primary-strong/--wss-color-error-strong tokens for AA text-on-fill contrast.\n\nCHANGED\n- --wss-color-text-deemphasized darkened to pass AA on hover; fixed control heights become min-height floors (WCAG 1.4.4) so a host page's own resets can't clamp them.\n\nFIXED\n- Table: Enter on interactive content in a plain Column no longer double-fires OnRowClick; a synthesized click during Loading no longer bypasses the same guard the keyboard path already had.\n- Pickers: disabled calendar cells use aria-disabled instead of native disabled, so a run of disabled days can no longer trap or strand keyboard focus.\n\nFull changelog: https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls#changelog",
